8`t/// Document-level gesture surface that owns mouse/touch selection across all
9`t/// editable blocks.
10`t///
11`t/// Wraps the scrollable editor content. Pointer events are translated to
12`t/// [DocumentPosition]s via the [BlockGeometryRegistry], so a drag that starts
13`t/// in one block can extend the selection into a neighbouring block. This
14`t/// replaces the per-block gesture detectors that previously trapped drags
15`t/// inside a single [TextSelectionSurface].
16`t///
17`t/// Supports:
18`t/// - tap → place collapsed caret
19`t/// - drag → extend selection (cross-block), with auto-scroll near viewport edges
20`t/// - auto-scroll → every drag (touch or mouse) synchronously scrolls one step
21`t///   when the pointer enters the viewport edge band, so the list follows the
22`t///   drag. For mouse/pen, a per-frame [Ticker] *additionally* keeps scrolling
23`t///   while the pointer is held still near an edge, letting the user scroll
24`t///   past the visible area. (Touch selection past the viewport uses dedicated
25`t///   handles, tracked separately as C9.)
26`t/// - double-tap → select word
